    "body": "\n      <p class=\"drop-cap\">Welcome to the inaugural issue of <strong>Mex-Ahoy!</strong>. For years, international coverage of Mexico has swung between two simplistic extremes: sensationalist headlines focused solely on border turbulence, or glossy resort brochures that reduce a nation of 130 million people to margaritas on a white-sand beach.</p>\n\n      <p>We created this digital newspaper because we believe the reality of Mexico is infinitely richer, more nuanced, and vastly more captivating than either cliché allows. Whether you are an expatriate making your home here, an investor tracking North American industrial realignments, or simply an inquisitive traveler who has fallen under this country’s magnetic spell, you deserve journalism that treats Mexico with intelligence and respect.</p>\n\n      <blockquote class=\"newspaper-quote\">\n        <p>“Mex-Ahoy! is your compass. We look into the politics, the neighborhoods, the artisan workshops, and the culinary kitchens that define the soul of Mexico.”</p>\n      </blockquote>\n\n      <p>Our editorial charter rests on three cardinal principles: <em>clarity without condescension</em>, <em>cultural immersion with critical honesty</em>, and <em>practical utility for everyday life</em>. In every edition, expect sharp political analysis, reliable guidance on visas, legalities and living costs, evocative travel dispatches, and culinary investigations that go deep into Mexico’s terroirs.</p>\n\n      <p>Thank you for boarding this voyage with us. Grab a warm cup of Chiapas coffee or a fresh pan dulce, and enjoy Volume 1, Number 1 of Mex-Ahoy!.</p>\n    ",
